WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.464
Hi, I'm Daisy!

00:00:02.464 --> 00:00:05.204
MiMo-V2.6 Pro is a trillion-parameter open model.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:08.335
Here's how it's stored, trained and sped up.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:13.336
A trillion parameters, shipped in four bits, tuned by thirty RL steps,

00:00:13.336 --> 00:00:16.836
and served with a drafter that fills eight slots at once.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:20.666
Pro has seventy layers.

00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:24.664
Sixty see only a hundred and twenty-eight token window; ten are global,

00:00:24.664 --> 00:00:26.330
and buy back the reach.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.596
Each feed-forward holds three hundred and eighty-four experts, top eight, none shared.

00:00:31.596 --> 00:00:34.422
About forty-two billion parameters work per token.

00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:39.352
And the release is the four-bit checkpoint: five hundred and sixty-six gigabytes,

00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:40.856
not about two terabytes.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.802
The whole RL run is thirty optimizer steps, each on fifteen hundred

00:00:46.802 --> 00:00:49.129
and sixty-eight prompts, sixteen rollouts apiece.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:54.189
The router is frozen, so the experts re-tune inside the routing that pre-training learned.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:58.500
Pass or fail can't rank two passing answers, so passing runs are

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.094
ranked, and advantage moves toward the better ones.

00:01:02.383 --> 00:01:05.301
Fill the next eight positions with a mask token.

00:01:05.301 --> 00:01:09.840
A five-layer drafter reads them in one pass, guided by the target's hidden states.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.749
It drafts seven tokens, the target checks the block once, and keeps

00:01:14.749 --> 00:01:16.245
the longest matching prefix.

00:01:16.245 --> 00:01:17.741
Same quality, by construction.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:21.992
But a block is eight positions, so one target pass yields at

00:01:21.992 --> 00:01:25.503
most eight tokens: eight times fewer passes, not the claimed twenty.

00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:30.802
The part that will last is the RL release: about seven thousand

00:01:30.802 --> 00:01:32.861
graded environments, each with its verifier.

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:39.289
To recap: four-bit weights, thirty RL steps, and a drafter capped at eight.

00:01:39.709 --> 00:01:41.826
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.826 --> 00:01:42.431
I'm Daisy.

00:01:42.431 --> 00:01:42.733
Bye!
